Reflecting heightened investment in the clean energy transition and recent reactor life extension initiatives, the compound annual growth rate has been revised upward from 3.9% to 4.2%. Governments worldwide are reaffirming commitments to low carbon electricity portfolios, prompting new build projects in China, India and Eastern Europe while existing fleets undergo major mid life upgrades. Stricter safety standards following recent incidents have also spurred demand for advanced diagnostic tools and predictive maintenance analytics.
What Are Nuclear Plant Operations and Maintenance Services?
These services comprise a comprehensive suite of activities that ensure nuclear power plants deliver reliable baseload electricity while adhering to the highest safety and environmental standards. Core components include real time condition monitoring, systematic preventive maintenance, component refurbishment, waste management, emergency response capabilities, and compliance reporting to nuclear regulatory authorities.
Key Market Drivers
Energy Security and Decarbonization Policies
The global push for carbon neutral electricity has reinforced nuclear power’s role as a dependable baseload source. Incentives across North America, Europe and Asia encourage operators to secure high performance O&M contracts that meet tightening emission targets.
Modernisation of Aging Reactor Fleets
More than 40% of the world’s reactors entered their third decade of operation in 2024. Aging equipment drives demand for predictive maintenance, component refurbishment and safety upgrades, creating a steady revenue stream for service providers. Proactive reliability programmes now outpace reactive repairs in most advanced markets.
