Competitive Landscape
Global Nuclear Plant Operations and Maintenance Services – Competitive Overview
The market is characterised by a high degree of fragmentation, with the three largest suppliers together accounting for only about 14 % of total revenue in 2023. China Huaneng leverages its extensive domestic generation portfolio to secure long term O&M contracts across the rapidly expanding Chinese nuclear fleet, while Orano’s fuel cycle expertise translates into integrated maintenance offerings throughout Europe and Africa. GE Hitachi Nuclear Energy distinguishes itself through advanced digital monitoring platforms that enable predictive maintenance, giving it a competitive edge in jurisdictions that prioritise technology driven safety upgrades.
Beyond the top tier, niche specialists shape dynamics through domain expertise and regional focus. BWX Technologies supplies critical components and on site repair services to North American reactors, whereas Westinghouse (Cameco) capitalises on its legacy reactor designs to win retrofit contracts in the United States and Canada. European vendors such as Veolia Nuclear Solutions and Worley command strong positions in waste handling and engineering integration projects across the EU. Firms like Bechtel, Mammoet and Fortum extend their construction and heavy lifting capabilities into O&M scopes, creating hybrid service models that appeal to operators seeking bundled solutions.
